--TEST--
`Stringable` is the only route from an object to a string, and an interpolation of one that lacks it is refused — `rule:classes/stringable`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:classes/stringable
class Point {
    public int $x;

    public function constructor(int $x) {
        $this->x = $x;
    }
}
var $p = new Point(1);
echo "point $p\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0412]: `Point` cannot be converted to `string` here; it does not implement `Stringable`
   --> case.nvs:11:13
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
